WEBVTT

00:15.432 --> 00:17.851
I can't believe you got a boyfriend.

00:17.934 --> 00:20.687
- Huh?
- What's wrong with that guy?

00:20.770 --> 00:23.648
He's delusional if he can't tell you're
a gorilla.

00:23.732 --> 00:24.774
What?!

00:25.734 --> 00:28.278
Sounds like maybe you're just jealous
of him.

00:28.361 --> 00:31.698
Keep it up and he's gonna see how weird
you are and dump you.

00:32.198 --> 00:35.910
Come and say that once you finally have
a successful relationship yourself.

00:35.994 --> 00:38.079
Although, I doubt you ever will.

00:40.707 --> 00:41.583
Shut up.

00:45.795 --> 00:46.713
Hey, don't worry!

00:48.048 --> 00:49.049
You piss me off!

00:49.758 --> 00:52.635
I THINK WE SHOULD BREAK UP

00:56.681 --> 00:57.682
I THINK WE SHOULD BREAK UP

00:57.766 --> 00:58.600
Why?

01:01.728 --> 01:02.687
Did I do something?

01:07.442 --> 01:10.528
He hasn't read my texts. What?
I'm blocked?

01:12.072 --> 01:13.823
It's all over!

01:16.701 --> 01:19.037
It's always over before it really begins.

01:19.913 --> 01:23.041
I wonder what he even liked about me
in the first place.

01:23.583 --> 01:24.959
He barely got to know me.

01:28.463 --> 01:31.758
Meanwhile, Koyun's been in a relationship
for so long.

01:31.841 --> 01:33.051
I'm kinda jealous.

01:35.220 --> 01:38.723
Tell me, Koyun, what is it you don't
like about Igarashi?

01:39.724 --> 01:40.558
Huh?

01:40.642 --> 01:43.645
I bet... there is a lot about him you can't
stand.

01:43.728 --> 01:44.562
AZUMI

01:44.646 --> 01:47.398
But he seems to really like you.

01:48.149 --> 01:51.027
Be glad someone likes you and stop
taking it for granted.

01:52.946 --> 01:53.905
Good point.

01:54.447 --> 01:57.325
I should be grateful that someone
even likes me.

01:58.618 --> 02:01.579
What if Igarashi's the only guy
out there...

02:02.080 --> 02:03.915
Who'll keep liking me.

02:04.707 --> 02:05.542
Koyun?

02:07.961 --> 02:09.295
So, where should we go next?

02:09.379 --> 02:10.296
Karaoke?

02:10.380 --> 02:11.756
Mmm, sure why not.

02:12.257 --> 02:15.093
- Could be fun.
- After that, Koyun dropped her club

02:15.176 --> 02:18.054
activities, and started dating Igarashi.

02:19.347 --> 02:22.308
I really wish I had never said
that to her.

02:23.393 --> 02:26.271
Be glad someone likes you and stop
taking it for granted.

02:27.147 --> 02:30.692
Does that mean this whole thing was my
fault?

03:56.361 --> 03:58.696
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

04:02.867 --> 04:06.871
New Semester

04:09.082 --> 04:11.292
Ugh. This year's almost over.

04:11.793 --> 04:13.253
AMAMIYA RESIDENCE
LIVING ROOM

04:13.336 --> 04:15.964
He's probably sad the seniors are
graduating, right?

04:17.131 --> 04:18.466
No! That's not it!

04:18.549 --> 04:20.134
Why're you whining? Ah, the band girl?

04:20.218 --> 04:21.219
- THIRD YEAR
- Yup.

04:21.302 --> 04:23.012
I said that's not it!

04:23.513 --> 04:25.056
Just tell her how you feel.

04:25.139 --> 04:26.182
Sure.

04:26.266 --> 04:27.267
Yeah' well...

04:27.350 --> 04:30.270
You of all people will never understand
how I feel, alright?

04:30.353 --> 04:31.938
Hm, so you admit it, Hayato.

04:32.021 --> 04:33.523
I totally understand.

04:34.023 --> 04:35.233
Uh, no you don't!

04:35.858 --> 04:38.319
You've never been in love with anyone
before.

04:39.279 --> 04:40.571
Wow! That was rude.

04:41.072 --> 04:44.575
I'll have you know, I've always
liked people as much as they liked me.

04:44.659 --> 04:47.662
- That's exactly what I'm talking about!
- That's exactly what I'm talking about!

04:47.745 --> 04:49.539
That's just you not disliking anyone.

04:49.622 --> 04:50.999
Isn't that a good thing?

04:51.082 --> 04:52.333
I don't get why it's bad.

04:52.834 --> 04:53.876
It is bad.

04:53.960 --> 04:57.088
And that's why you don't freaking
react to getting dumped.

04:57.171 --> 05:00.842
Well, me getting depressed or not isn't
gonna change the fact they wanted

05:00.925 --> 05:02.635
to break up with me, y'know?

05:03.136 --> 05:04.262
Ugh...

05:04.345 --> 05:06.389
Drive me nuts, you know that?

05:06.889 --> 05:09.642
Someday, when you finally fall in love
with someone...

05:10.435 --> 05:13.938
And they don't care about you at all,
I hope it really pushes you over

05:14.022 --> 05:15.064
the deep end, man.

05:15.148 --> 05:16.024
Same!

05:16.107 --> 05:17.483
We're friends, right?

05:18.484 --> 05:20.194
See? Aren't they mean?

05:20.987 --> 05:21.821
Mm.

05:23.990 --> 05:26.492
Oh, I made her laugh.

05:27.827 --> 05:28.661
It's so cute.

05:28.745 --> 05:29.579
STARE

05:31.497 --> 05:32.957
AMAMIYA RESIDENCE
LIVING ROOM

05:33.041 --> 05:33.875
Ugh.

05:35.543 --> 05:37.670
I wouldn't do something so pointless
anyway.

05:37.754 --> 05:39.255
- I thought so.
- I thought so.

05:41.299 --> 05:42.425
Emotions...

05:43.676 --> 05:45.094
The more you show them...

05:45.178 --> 05:47.263
The more it puts you at a disadvantage.

05:51.059 --> 05:53.311
And it makes you more vulnerable.

05:58.775 --> 06:00.818
You know, I've always wondered.

06:01.819 --> 06:05.281
You tell me to set goals, but then you
stop me from chasing my dreams?!

06:05.365 --> 06:07.825
I can tell you're not being serious
about this.

06:08.326 --> 06:10.286
Anyway, aren't you just moving
out to mess around?

06:10.370 --> 06:11.371
I can't believe this!

06:11.454 --> 06:14.332
What the hell? You don't know what you're
talking about, you old bastard.

06:14.415 --> 06:15.249
Ah, they're so loud.

06:15.333 --> 06:18.252
He's nothing but a troublemaker.
Wish he'd leave already.

06:18.753 --> 06:21.005
People get emotional and argue.

06:21.964 --> 06:24.675
What feelings could make people go
that far?

06:26.511 --> 06:29.055
Emotions are just a product of your mind, right?

06:30.098 --> 06:32.183
So shouldn't you be able to control them?

06:36.396 --> 06:37.814
Whoa. Hey, hold on!

06:41.275 --> 06:42.110
Hikawa!

06:44.320 --> 06:45.154
Ah...

06:47.949 --> 06:50.410
Oh, I... I'm so sorry, Miss.

06:53.246 --> 06:55.706
No! No, no, no!

06:57.708 --> 06:59.544
Alright, calm it down, brain!

06:59.627 --> 07:01.796
Do it. Do it!

07:02.296 --> 07:05.883
SOFT BREATHING

07:05.967 --> 07:06.843
A sea slug?

07:07.635 --> 07:09.929
Oh, yeah! Mm-hm. Looking good!

07:10.012 --> 07:11.556
Mm. Look here, now here.

07:11.639 --> 07:13.057
Wow! Hm?

07:13.141 --> 07:14.434
You free the day after tomorrow?

07:14.517 --> 07:15.351
Yota?

07:19.480 --> 07:21.524
Sorry, I have practice all day.

07:21.607 --> 07:22.900
Roger that.

07:25.778 --> 07:27.572
- Yota.
- Huh?

07:28.656 --> 07:29.824
Did I keep you waiting?

07:30.825 --> 07:31.659
Not at all.

07:32.452 --> 07:34.245
You're pretty easy to spot.

07:34.954 --> 07:35.872
Well, that's good.

07:36.497 --> 07:38.416
PUFFY FLUFFY

07:38.499 --> 07:41.002
- And you're all puffy, Yota.
- You're all fluffy.

07:41.085 --> 07:42.503
Sorry to drag you with me.

07:43.004 --> 07:44.005
It's fine.

07:44.088 --> 07:46.757
I've also been wanting to see where
Miki works.

07:46.841 --> 07:48.759
I know it's hard to go alone.

07:49.677 --> 07:51.804
I marked the location here on the map.

07:52.388 --> 07:53.890
Wow! You're so prepared.

07:54.432 --> 07:55.266
Hmm.

07:56.142 --> 07:57.810
- This way.
- Why, thank you.

07:59.145 --> 08:01.063
DREAM DREAM BURGER

08:02.356 --> 08:03.274
Hi, welcome...

08:03.357 --> 08:04.775
Oh! Hey, you guys!

08:05.276 --> 08:08.279
HUFF, HUFF

08:08.362 --> 08:09.238
What happened to you?

08:09.322 --> 08:11.657
We... we wandered around for thirty
minutes.

08:12.158 --> 08:15.203
What? Why?
It's only five minutes from the station.

08:15.828 --> 08:18.122
- Hm?
- I think it's the other way, Koyun.

08:18.623 --> 08:19.624
What?

08:20.625 --> 08:23.002
Sorry for asking you to come at such a
weird time.

08:23.085 --> 08:26.172
- Thank you.
- I- I can't really talk 'til after lunch.

08:27.173 --> 08:30.635
This is the most popular one, but I
personally recommend the one with

08:30.718 --> 08:31.719
avocado.

08:32.386 --> 08:33.846
Yota, you'll like this one.

08:33.930 --> 08:34.805
It's spicy!

08:34.889 --> 08:36.265
That's what I'll get.

08:36.349 --> 08:37.308
Oh, wow!

08:37.391 --> 08:39.310
Uh, hold on a sec.

08:39.393 --> 08:41.229
Take your time, don't worry!

08:42.271 --> 08:43.564
I'll get... the avocado.

08:44.065 --> 08:46.192
Okay. Order in!

08:46.275 --> 08:47.610
A chili and an avocado!

08:47.693 --> 08:50.154
- Okay.
- Hey, Miki.

08:51.531 --> 08:53.199
Are they in a relationship?

08:53.282 --> 08:54.200
Huh?

08:54.283 --> 08:56.786
No way. They're not dating.
We're all just friends.

08:56.869 --> 08:57.954
Oh, really?

08:58.621 --> 09:02.708
I mean... they just look really
cute together, is all.

09:03.459 --> 09:06.462
- Huh?
- The short girl with the tall guy.

09:06.546 --> 09:07.380
Look at that.

09:08.005 --> 09:09.215
Aren't they a cute pair?

09:10.216 --> 09:11.801
So heartwarming, gives me the feels.

09:11.884 --> 09:13.219
Yota and Koyun.

09:14.762 --> 09:17.473
It's literally never crossed my
mind until now.

09:18.099 --> 09:20.560
But if those two started dating...

09:21.435 --> 09:22.979
What would I do?

09:25.398 --> 09:26.941
Support the heck out of them.

09:27.024 --> 09:28.859
That'd be good... really good!

09:28.943 --> 09:31.988
Koyun would be way happier if she dated
someone like Yota.

09:33.322 --> 09:34.156
Don't need one.

09:34.240 --> 09:36.284
Ugh, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

09:36.367 --> 09:37.702
I've learned my lesson.

09:37.785 --> 09:40.204
I shouldn't meddle in her love
life anymore.

09:40.288 --> 09:41.330
Hm?

09:44.000 --> 09:45.585
How do I eat this?

09:47.086 --> 09:49.422
There's no way this'll fit in my
mouth, right?

09:50.673 --> 09:52.758
AH LAUGH

09:54.051 --> 09:55.469
Huh? What's so funny?

09:56.596 --> 09:59.599
Yeah. This is a great idea!

10:00.182 --> 10:02.518
- AMAMIYA
- I'm home.

10:04.103 --> 10:06.147
- Welcome back.
- Oh, you're home too.

10:06.647 --> 10:08.149
What about your job?

10:08.232 --> 10:10.276
- I got off early today.
- Oh!

10:10.776 --> 10:13.446
Check out this picture of Ponta
looking like a sea slug.

10:13.529 --> 10:15.197
Wow, that's so cute!

10:16.157 --> 10:17.783
Send it to me when you get a sec.

10:17.867 --> 10:18.743
Okay.

10:19.243 --> 10:21.537
Um, let's see, where's our text thread?

10:22.622 --> 10:24.790
Huh? Yota has a profile pic now?

10:25.291 --> 10:26.459
He never does.

10:27.752 --> 10:28.836
A hamburger?

10:30.463 --> 10:31.297
Hm?

10:33.549 --> 10:34.383
Ugh!

10:37.345 --> 10:39.221
Ahh... What?

10:39.722 --> 10:41.140
Minato, you sent it yet?

10:41.849 --> 10:43.392
Uh, what're you doing?

10:43.976 --> 10:47.063
What in the world... is going on?

10:53.861 --> 10:54.820
I knew it!

10:54.904 --> 10:57.365
Yota and Hikawa are...

11:00.034 --> 11:02.078
GRADE 1 CLASS 6

11:02.161 --> 11:03.788
Winter break ended too soon.

11:04.497 --> 11:05.998
Yota, your profile pic...

11:06.499 --> 11:07.583
What's the deal?

11:08.376 --> 11:10.544
Huh? Oh, my profile?

11:11.671 --> 11:13.464
It's the same one Koyun has.

11:13.547 --> 11:14.382
CASUALLY

11:14.465 --> 11:16.133
- Miki drew it.
- Wait a sec, Miki?

11:17.802 --> 11:23.474
PRAISE ME

11:24.058 --> 11:25.601
The Alive Burger is really cute.

11:25.685 --> 11:27.436
I love all the compliments!

11:27.520 --> 11:28.479
Yeah.

11:28.562 --> 11:30.731
I learned that when Koyun and I went to
Miki's job.

11:30.815 --> 11:31.649
CRACK

11:31.732 --> 11:32.566
Just... you two?

11:33.567 --> 11:37.405
Yeah. Remember I asked if you were free,
but you said you had club activities.

11:37.488 --> 11:40.116
Ugh! Now that you mention it...

11:41.701 --> 11:44.453
The moral of the story is to be
considerate by telling people

11:44.537 --> 11:46.080
what you're inviting them to!

11:47.206 --> 11:49.250
- Yota.
- Huh?

11:50.126 --> 11:51.836
Being left out is lonely.

11:52.336 --> 11:55.089
You saying how you actually feel is very
creepy.

11:55.172 --> 11:57.717
GRADE 1 CLASS 2

11:57.800 --> 12:01.095
So, we still haven't decided who's on the
library committee.

12:01.178 --> 12:02.012
That's harsh.

12:03.639 --> 12:05.558
Winter break flew by cause I was stuck
working.

12:05.641 --> 12:08.269
The library committee eats up a
lot of after school time, doesn't it?

12:08.352 --> 12:10.312
- Yeah, I absolutely don't wanna be on it.
- But work was so slow.

12:10.396 --> 12:13.149
The shifts are flexible, the customers
are chill and also not my age, so

12:13.232 --> 12:15.067
- it's the best job I could ask for.
- I'm already a class rep.

12:15.151 --> 12:16.861
I can't take time off from my club.

12:16.944 --> 12:18.112
I hope I never lose it.

12:19.029 --> 12:22.533
Anyone not in a club and not on
a committee yet?

12:23.534 --> 12:24.368
Hm?

12:31.333 --> 12:32.168
Huh?

12:32.251 --> 12:34.044
LIBRARY COMMITTEE (2)
SHIMOJIMA, HIKAWA

12:34.128 --> 12:35.087
HIKAWA

12:35.171 --> 12:36.005
BOOM!

12:38.924 --> 12:40.551
It seems like there's a lot to do.

12:40.634 --> 12:43.637
When we're on reception duty, we
have to stay until everyone

12:43.721 --> 12:44.555
else goes home.

12:45.097 --> 12:46.474
SILENCE

12:47.266 --> 12:48.601
The silence is awkward.

12:51.145 --> 12:53.105
I have to change my work shifts.

12:54.023 --> 12:54.857
Hm?

12:55.399 --> 12:58.068
Oh, so you're not in a club either,
Shimojima?

12:58.569 --> 13:01.155
Huh? Oh, no, I'm in the art club!

13:01.739 --> 13:05.326
Uh, um, but, well, since I just kinda
draw whatever I want, people tend

13:06.035 --> 13:08.537
to think I have it easy, or how should I
put it...

13:10.122 --> 13:13.501
PISSES ME OFF, PISSES ME OFF,
PISSES ME OFF, PISSES ME OFF

13:13.584 --> 13:14.418
do nothing and have tons of free time
on our hands.

13:14.502 --> 13:17.713
All the jocks in sports clubs
think us art kids sit around and

13:17.797 --> 13:19.381
Oh no! Did I vent too much?

13:20.800 --> 13:21.801
I'm mad...

13:23.344 --> 13:26.180
At those who make assumptions and look
down on others.

13:26.680 --> 13:27.515
Huh?

13:28.182 --> 13:31.101
I didn't think that kind of stuff
happened at this school.

13:31.936 --> 13:34.021
Huh? Did she just agree?

13:35.064 --> 13:35.981
With me?

13:36.816 --> 13:37.650
Hm?

13:38.567 --> 13:39.401
Wait.

13:41.237 --> 13:42.863
- Sorry.
- Huh?

13:42.947 --> 13:44.406
I'm going that way for a bit.

13:45.115 --> 13:46.075
Yeah, sure.

13:46.659 --> 13:47.535
See ya.

13:48.869 --> 13:50.246
Oh. Okay, see ya.

13:51.497 --> 13:54.792
Hikawa really wasn't as scary as I
thought.

13:57.878 --> 13:58.712
Yota!

14:00.005 --> 14:00.840
Koyun.

14:02.800 --> 14:03.634
Ah.

14:04.510 --> 14:07.263
- Happy New Year, my friend.
- Happy New Year, my friend.

14:11.100 --> 14:12.309
What about your club?

14:13.143 --> 14:14.103
We have the day off.

14:14.186 --> 14:16.188
We can't use the gym today.

14:16.272 --> 14:17.106
Gotcha.

14:18.065 --> 14:20.067
Wait. Have you been here all this time?

14:20.150 --> 14:21.026
Yep.

14:21.527 --> 14:25.489
I like to zone out sometimes and
just look up at the sky.

14:26.365 --> 14:27.199
Oh.

14:27.908 --> 14:29.660
So, you got something on your mind?

14:30.494 --> 14:31.912
No. That's not it.

14:33.539 --> 14:35.040
I don't think about anything.

14:38.460 --> 14:39.295
I see.

14:42.590 --> 14:43.424
So peaceful.

14:44.508 --> 14:47.344
Both this location, and Yota himself.

14:49.054 --> 14:50.264
He's so relaxed.

14:51.056 --> 14:52.558
Like a passing cloud.

14:54.476 --> 14:56.812
Well, he's so tall his head's
basically in them.

14:56.896 --> 14:57.897
HEH HEH

14:59.231 --> 15:01.400
Not thinking about anything is hard.

15:03.819 --> 15:06.739
I'm always thinking about something,
usually worrying.

15:07.615 --> 15:10.200
Or getting angry over trivial things.

15:11.160 --> 15:13.162
An annoying habit of mine.

15:15.664 --> 15:17.166
I'm the total opposite of him.

15:19.585 --> 15:22.671
I can't imagine Yota letting himself
get bent out of shape.

15:22.755 --> 15:25.633
Or worrying about anything the way I do.

15:28.719 --> 15:29.637
That's nice.

15:31.263 --> 15:32.806
I wanna be more like him.

15:38.687 --> 15:42.191
- Agh.
- Yo, Amamiya, pay attention, would ya!

15:42.900 --> 15:43.776
Those two?

15:44.318 --> 15:45.152
Seriously?

15:54.370 --> 15:56.330
Well, I finished that one too.

15:57.373 --> 15:59.500
There're fewer people here than I
thought.

16:01.210 --> 16:02.086
An art book?

16:02.169 --> 16:05.547
Y-Yeah. I can learn a lot from reading it.

16:06.048 --> 16:07.967
But you're already so good at drawing.

16:08.467 --> 16:10.010
No, no, I'm not that good.

16:10.511 --> 16:12.596
Wait, what? Have you seen my drawings?

16:12.680 --> 16:13.722
Oh, yeah.

16:13.806 --> 16:18.143
When we were doing oil paintings,
I could see it from where I was sitting.

16:19.937 --> 16:22.439
- Sorry! I looked without asking.
- Swish.

16:22.523 --> 16:24.733
What? It's fine, it's fine. Come back.

16:28.278 --> 16:30.280
- See ya!
- See ya later.

16:33.450 --> 16:35.786
Maybe I should look at some art
books too.

16:36.412 --> 16:38.497
I wonder which one I should start with.

16:38.580 --> 16:40.290
GROWL

16:43.293 --> 16:44.128
Huh?

16:47.131 --> 16:48.716
He's easy to spot.

16:50.300 --> 16:52.052
CLEARLY YOTA

16:53.846 --> 16:55.723
- THUD
- Oh, sorry!

16:56.223 --> 16:57.266
Oh! Koyun.

16:57.766 --> 16:59.351
You scared me.

17:01.687 --> 17:04.898
Don't you know how dangerous it is to be
in my blind spot?

17:04.982 --> 17:06.900
You make it sound like you're a truck.

17:12.948 --> 17:14.867
What're you doin' here? Ah, same here.

17:15.534 --> 17:17.036
Are you in a hurry?

17:18.245 --> 17:19.079
Hm?

17:23.125 --> 17:24.543
It's warming my hands up.

17:26.336 --> 17:27.421
It's gonna get cold.

17:27.921 --> 17:29.381
Don't you have dinner at home?

17:29.465 --> 17:30.507
What about that?

17:31.091 --> 17:32.468
Oh no, it's fine.

17:35.012 --> 17:36.430
I can manage both just fine.

17:37.347 --> 17:38.182
Figures.

17:38.891 --> 17:42.144
I noticed you've been staying late
after school recently.

17:42.227 --> 17:44.730
Oh, I'm on library duty right now.

17:45.230 --> 17:47.483
Ah, they forced it on you?

17:48.484 --> 17:50.069
That's not what happened.

17:50.986 --> 17:53.238
Hm? Wait, is that what happened?

17:55.908 --> 17:59.912
Although I've become interested in
things I'd never been exposed to before.

17:59.995 --> 18:01.455
So it's not all that bad.

18:01.538 --> 18:02.372
Or not yet.

18:03.165 --> 18:04.625
And I have time to daydream.

18:05.167 --> 18:06.001
Oh, really?

18:06.085 --> 18:08.462
I should've picked library committee too, then.

18:09.588 --> 18:11.924
Your club activities don't leave you any
time.

18:12.633 --> 18:13.467
Hmm.

18:14.802 --> 18:17.638
But spending my time daydreaming
sounds nice.

18:20.516 --> 18:21.892
Talking with Yota...

18:22.643 --> 18:24.103
I feel so at ease.

18:26.855 --> 18:27.689
It feels warm.

18:36.073 --> 18:38.075
The fries aren't salty enough today.

18:38.158 --> 18:40.786
- Huh? Mine are really good.
- Hikawa and Yota.

18:45.040 --> 18:46.416
I wish they wouldn't.

18:49.753 --> 18:52.047
Because if you fall in love with Yota...

18:52.131 --> 18:54.007
You'll just end up getting hurt.

18:59.680 --> 19:01.265
Isn't your house that way, Yota?

19:01.348 --> 19:02.349
Yeah.

19:02.432 --> 19:04.351
But I'll walk you to the station.

19:04.434 --> 19:05.644
Oh, you don't have to.

19:06.145 --> 19:08.814
I'm just kinda worried you'll get lost.

19:08.897 --> 19:10.107
I won't get lost.

19:13.986 --> 19:14.820
Yota!

19:18.991 --> 19:20.742
Agh! That scared me.

19:20.826 --> 19:23.328
Turn on your lights. Jeez.

19:26.957 --> 19:29.251
- Are you okay?
- Y- Yeah.

19:29.835 --> 19:30.669
Sorry.

19:31.503 --> 19:32.671
Here, hold on to me.

19:33.922 --> 19:34.798
There you go.

19:47.269 --> 19:48.228
Is something wrong?

19:49.229 --> 19:50.898
Huh? Uh, no.

19:51.773 --> 19:52.608
Just now...

19:54.359 --> 19:56.320
It reminded me of when I was a kid.

19:57.529 --> 20:00.115
I-I suddenly remembered my dad.

20:01.241 --> 20:02.701
It felt floaty.

20:02.784 --> 20:05.996
- FLOATY
- Wait, what am I even saying?

20:08.415 --> 20:11.084
Then I'll let it slide if you
accidentally call me Dad.

20:11.168 --> 20:14.004
That's what elementary school kids
do to their teachers.

20:17.758 --> 20:18.842
I see now.

20:19.468 --> 20:20.594
That's why they do it.

20:22.763 --> 20:25.224
I wonder... how my dad's doing.

20:30.312 --> 20:33.649
If you were my kid, I'd have to go to the
Lost Child Center every time you left

20:33.732 --> 20:34.566
the house.

20:34.650 --> 20:37.236
I told you I wouldn't get lost
every time.

20:39.738 --> 20:40.572
Yota, hi!

20:41.281 --> 20:42.115
Huh?

20:49.790 --> 20:50.666
Why're you here?

20:51.792 --> 20:53.418
I forgot something at the store.

20:54.544 --> 20:56.088
And Haruto and Sakura?

20:57.089 --> 20:58.966
Oh, your dad's at home with them.

20:59.049 --> 21:01.385
Oh, so he got home early today.

21:01.468 --> 21:02.844
I'm assuming you already had dinner?

21:02.928 --> 21:03.762
A family member?

21:03.845 --> 21:05.847
I didn't actually. Sorry I didn't
reach out sooner.

21:05.931 --> 21:08.892
Is she his sister?
I'm wondering if maybe I should go home.

21:09.893 --> 21:12.104
- Yota.
- Well, be there soon.

21:12.187 --> 21:14.189
I- I'm walking my friend to the station.

21:14.940 --> 21:15.774
Huh?

21:16.942 --> 21:17.985
Oh, okay.

21:18.777 --> 21:19.611
Be careful.

21:32.499 --> 21:34.001
Yota, everything okay?

21:34.501 --> 21:35.627
Hm?

21:35.711 --> 21:36.545
With, um...

21:37.421 --> 21:38.255
Well...

21:38.755 --> 21:40.465
- Your sist-
- My mom.

21:41.258 --> 21:42.092
Huh?

21:43.343 --> 21:45.887
That woman is my mother.

21:46.638 --> 21:50.183
?? YEARS OLD - 16 YEARS OLD = ??

21:52.060 --> 21:53.770
Not related by blood, obviously.

21:55.272 --> 21:58.650
My real mother died when I was in
elementary school.

22:06.158 --> 22:08.618
Oh, I'm sorry. That's the normal reaction.

22:08.702 --> 22:09.828
Oh. No...

22:11.330 --> 22:13.749
It, it happened a long time ago, so I'm
fine.

22:14.916 --> 22:15.792
And well now...

22:17.002 --> 22:18.295
They're my real family.
